<title>USA: J.C. Penney, Eckerd deal clears antitrust review.</title>
<headline>J.C. Penney, Eckerd deal clears antitrust review.</headline>
<dateline>PLANO, Texas 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>J. C. Penney Co Inc said its proposed $3.3 billion acquisition of Eckerd Corp cleared the Hart-Scott-Rodino Act antitrust waiting period.</p>
<p>The U.S. Federal Trade Commission also indicated that it will not extend the waiting period by requesting additional information about the deal, J.C. Penney said.</p>
<p>J.C. Penney also said it reached a satisfactory agreement, subject to FTC approval, involving a divestiture of some stores. The details of the divestitures will be released upon regulatory approval, the retailer said.</p>
<p>J.C. Penney said it plans to proceed with its cash tender offer for about 35.3 million Eckerd shares. The tender offer is scheduled to expire at midnight on December 6.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
